xnu 0116: say whether the timer interrupt ever leaves the timer

Every timed wait on this board hangs: the sampler thread's tsleep() never
wakes, the timer beacon is never painted, and userland's usleep() never
returns (which is also why _detectDisplays never does). The timer is armed
(CNTV_CTL reads ENABLE, CVAL sits just ahead of CNTVCT), so the question is
where the interrupt is lost.

End and drop the PPI before enabling it -- an interrupt the loader left active
can never be taken again -- and clear its Group 1 secure modifier, which would
keep it away from EL1 entirely. Print the live PPI state (pending/active), the
count of timer interrupts the CPU actually took, DAIF and the CPU interface's
group/priority mask with the CNTV registers. Print the GIC and IRQ dumps with
printf instead of kprintf so the panel and the ring see them at all, and wake
the ring every 8 KiB so those lines arrive during boot instead of once.

